From df56a9229ea963fb1c06b436355e42360eb450e8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: William Emerison Six <billsix@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 12:34:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 42/46] game: set the tilting pyramid's marioOnPlatform flag
 instead of incrementing it

`marioOnPlatform` starts FALSE and is tested with `if (marioOnPlatform)`;
the `++` that turns it on is a boolean assignment written for a MIPS
`addiu`.

Verified: tilting_inverted_pyramid.inc.c, through its including
translation unit, compiles to byte-identical assembly before and after
with the port's own flags (asmdiff over compile_commands.json).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/game/behaviors/tilting_inverted_pyramid.inc.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/game/behaviors/tilting_inverted_pyramid.inc.c b/src/game/behaviors/tilting_inverted_pyramid.inc.c
index 062a8310..b686011a 100644
--- a/src/game/behaviors/tilting_inverted_pyramid.inc.c
+++ b/src/game/behaviors/tilting_inverted_pyramid.inc.c
@@ -107,7 +107,7 @@ void bhv_tilting_inverted_pyramid_loop(void) {
         }
 
         if (o->oTiltingPyramidMarioOnPlatform == TRUE) {
-            marioOnPlatform++;
+            marioOnPlatform = TRUE;
         }
 
         o->oTiltingPyramidMarioOnPlatform = TRUE;
-- 
